WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.700
We get it — sometimes, kid-friendly films
are just plain unbearable for adults.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.010
Filmmakers understand this too, and often
try to add things that make being trapped

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.710
in a theater with a hundred sniffling kids
more tolerable.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:14.480
Occasionally, however, they go a little too
far.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.039
Here are a few adult jokes we can't believe
they allowed in kids movies.

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:20.039
Inside Out

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:25.200
Pixar's 2015 animated feature Inside Out was
obviously kid-friendly, being Pixar and all.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.340
There was, however, one joke that pushed the
envelope just a bit.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.340
"What was that?

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.619
Was it a bear, it's a bear?"

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:32.220
"There are no bears in San Francisco."

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.750
"I saw a really hairy guy, he looked like
a bear."

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.660
If you've ever taken a stroll through the
Castro District in San Francisco, you probably

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.210
know exactly what Anger is talking about.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:43.460
"Everybody bottoms up."

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.970
"Bottoms up"

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.690
Aladdin and The King of Thieves

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.420
In the third installment of Disney's Aladdin
franchise, our hero finally gets the girl.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.420
Since this was a direct-to-video production,
Robin Williams, who returned as the hilarious

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.990
Genie, made a bawdy joke that maybe shouldn't
have made it past the editors.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:03.710
"I thought the earth wasn't suppose to move
until the honeymoon."

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:04.750
Get it?

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:05.790
Yeah...you get it.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:09.240
And of course, this wouldn't be the first
time Disney got a little frisky.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.450
Mrs. Doubtfire

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.740
Robin Williams was given free rein when it
came to his improvizations in Mrs. Doubtfire,

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.650
with the understanding that the final film
would be cut to a still-family friendly, if

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:20.710
a little cheeky, PG-13 rating.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:25.390
Williams got so risqué with his off-the-wall
freestyling that there's another unseen version

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:27.820
of the movie which is rated NC-17.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:31.030
We're not sure how much more suggestive it
can get than this, however.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.920
"A bit of a going down payment, hm?"

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.040
"Excuse me?"

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:42.710
"You know dear, sink the sub, hide the weasel,
pop the porpoise, bit of the old humpty dumpty,

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:46.600
little jack horny, the horizontal mumbo, hm."

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:47.760
"Mrs. Doubtfire"

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:54.690
"The bone dancer, rumpleforskin, baloney bop,
bit of the old cunulinquistics, hm."

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.430
"Mrs. Doubtfire, please."

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:57.430
Scooby-Doo

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:01.490
In the live-action adaptation of Scooby-Doo,
the gang takes a flight to Spooky Island.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:06.860
Along the way, Shaggy finds himself unexpectedly
seated next to a blonde bombshell on the airplane,

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.280
who introduces herself.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.559
"I'm Marry Jane."

00:02:10.559 --> 00:02:12.819
"Like that is my favorite name."

00:02:12.819 --> 00:02:13.819
"Really"

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:14.819
"Yeah"

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:18.059
Thanks, Warner Brothers, for finally confirming
what fans have suspected all along.

00:02:18.059 --> 00:02:20.969
Now we know why Shaggy's always got the munchies…

00:02:20.969 --> 00:02:23.019
"Like wow, my favorite.

00:02:23.019 --> 00:02:28.510
A double triple decker sardine and marshmallow
fudge sandwich."

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.959
The Road to El Dorado

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:34.900
In this DreamWorks animated adventure, our
hero Tulio falls in love with the lovely Chel,

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.120
and the pair spend some quality time together.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.519
But in one particular scene, the film goes
from romantic to downright explicit.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.700
"Woah,"

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:47.040
"My lords, hello"

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:48.680
"The high priest"

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:49.940
"Oww"

00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:55.440
Sure does look like the animators were going
for something a little more serious than kissing.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.680
Muppet Treasure Island

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.069
It's in Muppet Treasure Island that we learn
Kermit the Frog's sometime-girlfriend, Miss

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:05.079
Piggy, or Benjamina Gunn in the context of
this film, has been seeing some other guys,

00:03:05.079 --> 00:03:06.609
like Long John Silver.

00:03:06.609 --> 00:03:08.680
Well, more than seeing.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:14.600
"This seems to be your day for renewing old
acquaintances."

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.540
"Well, hello Loooong John."

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.879
"Oh no, him too."

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:23.620
Thanks for that, Muppets.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.519
"Dad, what's a muppet?"

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:31.019
"Well, it's not quite a mop, it's not quite
a puppet but man, he he he he.

00:03:31.019 --> 00:03:33.709
So to answer your question, I don't know."

00:03:33.709 --> 00:03:35.620
The Brave Little Toaster to the Rescue

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:39.549
The writers behind The Brave Little Toaster
to the Rescue didn't even bother to hide this

00:03:39.549 --> 00:03:43.359
one, which comes complete with soft-jazz bedroom
music.

00:03:43.359 --> 00:03:44.620
"Wow"

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.300
"What's happening"

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.532
"Frikenstin is searching through all my files.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:54.120
Searching through regions here to for only
dreamed of by man.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.589
Wooo, that feels sorta good."

00:03:56.589 --> 00:03:57.589
"What does"

00:03:57.589 --> 00:04:02.099
"My memory banks are being stroked and by
an expert.

00:04:02.099 --> 00:04:10.790
I feel something, something happening inside
of me and I can't keep it to myself any longer."

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.159
Nope, your eyes and ears aren't fooling you.

00:04:13.159 --> 00:04:16.889
That was the grossest thing you've seen a
computer do all day.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:21.289
And considering what most computers are used
for these days, that's really saying something.

00:04:21.289 --> 00:04:22.960
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:28.259
During one notable scene in the 2014 Teenage
Mutant Ninja Turtles reboot, the huge, heroic

00:04:28.259 --> 00:04:30.740
reptiles are introduced to reporter April
O'Neil.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:35.030
As Raphael tries to get her to hand over the
photo she just snapped, we can hear this sleazy

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.030
remark….

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.870
"Oh, she's so hot I can feel my shell tightening."

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:40.900
"We can hear you."

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.740
We can hear him too.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.729
Time to wash our ears til they bleed!

00:04:44.729 --> 00:04:45.729
Thanks for watching!

00:04:45.729 --> 00:04:48.960
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.990
And leave us a comment to let us know your
favorite adult jokes in kids movies...

